  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> Baron’s Secluded Library</sup></p>\n<p><strong>Benefits:</strong> Whenever you target an attended item with a magic sphere effect or attack roll, you may have any number of the ability’s non-damaging effects apply to the attending creature rather than the item as long as the attending creature is an eligible target for these additional effects. For example, if you attack a weapon using a Fire Blast from the Destruction sphere, you may force the attended creature to attempt a Reflex save against catching fire rather than the item. Only a single creature may be considered “attending” a targeted item.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/combat-feats#toc11\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
